CM_ "MSEL Solid State Master Relay (Motorsport Electronics Ltd), CAN interface.

Authored in this repository from the Master Relay User's Manual Rev 2.0
(September 2025), https://msel.co.nz/content/MSEMR_User_Manual.pdf -- tables 5,
6, 7, 8, 9 and 10. It replaces the vendor's own MSEMR_CAN_Information_141119.dbc
(dated 2014-11-19), which is eleven years older than that manual and describes a
device that no longer matches: it has no 0x6E7 message, no value tables, and
signal ranges that contradict the specification (0-20 V on an 8-30 V device).

THE MESSAGE IDS HERE ARE THE FACTORY DEFAULTS, NOT CONSTANTS. The base CAN
address is user-configurable (manual, 'Changing the Base CAN Identifier'), and
these three messages sit at base+0, base+1 and base+3. Anything decoding a relay
that has been re-addressed must map the observed identifier back onto the
canonical one before dispatching; libs/msel_master_relay does exactly that, and
is the reason no consumer should match these numbers directly.

Three things the device does over CAN are deliberately absent here, because a
DBC cannot express them. The five configuration commands are constant-magic
frames on a fixed identifier (0x789) whose payload carries each value twice, a
redundancy no signal definition can check. The remote kill trigger is eight
constant bytes and has no signals at all. And the response to a configuration
command arrives on the base status identifier, sharing an id with the periodic
message above -- two different layouts on one id, which is precisely what a DBC
has no way to describe. All three live in libs/msel_master_relay/protocol.h,
next to the tests that pin them against the manual's worked examples.";

CM_ BO_ 1764 "Status and telemetry. Base address + 0, default 0x6E4.
Transmitted at 10Hz by default, 100Hz if the transmit rate is reconfigured.
All multi-byte channels are big-endian (MSB first). Manual table 5.";
CM_ SG_ 1764 status "Current device state. Manual table 8.";
CM_ SG_ 1764 CAN_kill "Warning bit 0x80: shut down by a remote CAN message.";
CM_ SG_ 1764 external_kill "Warning bit 0x40: external kill switch triggered.";
CM_ SG_ 1764 driver_kill "Warning bit 0x20: driver kill switch off.";
CM_ SG_ 1764 over_temp_kill "Warning bit 0x10: isolated at 110C.";
CM_ SG_ 1764 high_voltage_warn "Warning bit 0x08: above the 28V upper limit.";
CM_ SG_ 1764 low_voltage_warn "Warning bit 0x04: below the 7V lower limit.";
CM_ SG_ 1764 over_current_warn "Warning bit 0x02: over current.";
CM_ SG_ 1764 over_temp_warn "Warning bit 0x01: above the 90C warning limit.";
CM_ SG_ 1764 temperature_internal "Internal temperature. Sensitivity 0.2C,
calibration error +/-3C, specified over 0 to 125C.";
CM_ SG_ 1764 load_current "Current through the relay, positive when the battery
is discharging and negative when it is being charged. Accurate to +/-10% or 1A,
whichever is greater -- a total system draw indication, not a per-device
measurement. Specified over -255 to 600A.";
CM_ SG_ 1764 voltage_out "Voltage on the output terminal. The device operates
between 8 and 30V; the range given is what the 16-bit raw value can represent,
since the vendor specifies no narrower one.";

CM_ BO_ 1765 "Serial number, live configuration readback, and shutdown history.
Base address + 1, default 0x6E5. Manual table 6.";
CM_ SG_ 1765 shutdown_cause_2 "Cause of the second to last shutdown, using the
status enumeration. Only populated from serial number 61061 onward; earlier
units report the last event alone.";
CM_ SG_ 1765 shutdown_cause "Cause of the last shutdown, using the status
enumeration.";
CM_ SG_ 1765 time_since_shutdown "Time since the last shutdown event.";
CM_ SG_ 1765 config_shutdown_delay "How long power is held up after a shutdown
event, so data loggers can flush before the battery is isolated. Default 1.0s.
This is the one setting that takes effect without a power cycle. An over current
event ignores it and disconnects immediately.";
CM_ SG_ 1765 config_CAN_kill "Whether the device accepts a remote CAN shutdown.
Disabled from the factory. Manual table 10.";
CM_ SG_ 1765 config_CAN_baud "Configured bus rate. Changing this needs a power
cycle, and the rest of the bus has to move with it or the relay disappears.";
CM_ SG_ 1765 config_output_drive "PDM/ECU output drive configuration. Value 3 is
not assigned. Manual tables 2 and 21.";
CM_ SG_ 1765 serial_no "Serial number. 64666 and above (firmware 2.0F) also
transmit Master_Relay_Switch_State, and are identifiable by black torx drive
screws on the top of the unit.";
CM_ SG_ 1765 voltage_in "Voltage on the input (battery) terminal.";

CM_ BO_ 1767 "Current calibration and external switch mode. Base address + 3,
default 0x6E7. Only transmitted by units at serial number 64666 or above, so its
absence is normal on older hardware rather than a fault. Manual table 7.

Declared as 2 bytes because the manual documents only bytes 0 and 1. That is
also the safe choice: a message declared shorter than the device sends still
decodes, whereas one declared longer silently rejects every frame.";
CM_ SG_ 1767 current_switch_state "Manual table 9.";

VAL_ 1764 status 10 "Power_On_Reset" 9 "CAN_Trigger_Kill" 8 "External_Switch_Kill" 7 "Driver_Switch_Kill" 6 "Over_Temperature_Kill" 5 "High_Voltage_Warning" 4 "Low_Voltage_Warning" 3 "Over_Current_Warning" 2 "Over_Temperature_Warning" 1 "Normal";
VAL_ 1765 shutdown_cause 10 "Power_On_Reset" 9 "CAN_Trigger_Kill" 8 "External_Switch_Kill" 7 "Driver_Switch_Kill" 6 "Over_Temperature_Kill" 5 "High_Voltage_Warning" 4 "Low_Voltage_Warning" 3 "Over_Current_Warning" 2 "Over_Temperature_Warning" 1 "Normal";
VAL_ 1765 shutdown_cause_2 10 "Power_On_Reset" 9 "CAN_Trigger_Kill" 8 "External_Switch_Kill" 7 "Driver_Switch_Kill" 6 "Over_Temperature_Kill" 5 "High_Voltage_Warning" 4 "Low_Voltage_Warning" 3 "Over_Current_Warning" 2 "Over_Temperature_Warning" 1 "Normal";
VAL_ 1765 config_CAN_kill 2 "ADR" 1 "Enabled" 0 "Disabled";
VAL_ 1765 config_CAN_baud 2 "Baud_250_Kbps" 1 "Baud_500_Kbps" 0 "Baud_1_Mbps";
VAL_ 1765 config_output_drive 6 "Active_Lo_Low_Side" 5 "Active_Lo_High_Side" 4 "Active_Lo_Half_Bridge" 2 "Active_Hi_Low_Side" 1 "Active_Hi_High_Side" 0 "Active_Hi_Half_Bridge";
VAL_ 1767 current_switch_state 4 "Legacy_Cal_Internal_External_Switch" 3 "Legacy_Cal_Normal_External_Switch" 2 "Normal_Cal_Internal_External_Switch" 1 "Normal_Cal_Normal_External_Switch";
